{"abstract":"Recent studies focusing on the digitalization of welfare provision draw attention to digital infrastructures that produce new forms of social inequality and disempowerment due to inaccessibility. Against this backdrop, we study the practices of a Danish public library in supporting citizens with digital applications for welfare benefits. Through a grounded theory approach to data collection and analysis, we draw on ethnographic materials and Catriona Mackenzie’s multidimensional analysis of autonomy to conceptualize autonomy alliances and data care practices. These are collective efforts that attempt to subvert inaccessible and autonomy-undermining public digital infrastructures. Drawing on a relational view of autonomy, we examine how certain design choices can constrain citizens’ personal autonomy and equal access to welfare services. For this reason, we discuss the importance of studying political decisions affecting the design and organization of digital welfare services, as well as the local practices that compensate for discriminatory design choices through social inclusion and a commitment to equity.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Carreras, Barbara","Finken, Sisse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799128"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital Inclusion","Digital welfare","Equity","Inaccessibility","Public library","Relational autonomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomy alliances and data care practices","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.mendeley.com/catalogue/2377a4a5-f2c8-3eb3-8991-644d051e71f8/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799128","identifier":[{"id":"85138000310","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-27f412aa-099b-4abc-b1fd-e851434711e7"],"keyword":["Digital inclusion","Digital welfare","Equity","Inaccessibility","Public library","Relational autonomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-F84B934B688E73F4BB8E003353F7173F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Barbara Nino","key":"carreraspau","last":"Carreras","locid":"62c988d5-8eed-4ed3-8a53-aedace29e5bc","name":"Carreras, Barbara","name_org":"Carreras, Barbara Nino","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sisse","key":"finkenpau","last":"Finken","name":"Finken, Sisse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-15688-5_5","isbn":["9783031156878"],"pages":"47-57","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","series":"IFIP Advances in Information and Communication Technology","status":"p","title":"IFIP Advances in Information and Communication Technology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138000310"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-27f412aa-099b-4abc-b1fd-e851434711e7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Autonomy Alliances and Data Care Practices","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799128","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"IFIP International Conference on Human Choice and Computers HCC 2022: Human Choice and Digital by Default: Autonomy vs Digital Determination pp 47–57Cite as Autonomy Alliances and Data Care Practices Barbara Nino Carreras & Sisse Finken Conference paper First Online: 30 August 2022 138 Accesses 2 Altmetric Part of the IFIP Advances in Information and Communication Technology book series (IFIPAICT,volume 656) Abstract Recent studies focusing on the digitalization of welfare provision draw attention to digital infrastructures that produce new forms of social inequality and disempowerment due to inaccessibility. Against this backdrop, we study the practices of a Danish public library in supporting citizens with digital applications for welfare benefits. Through a grounded theory approach to data collection and analysis, we draw on ethnographic materials and Catriona Mackenzie’s multidimensional analysis of autonomy to conceptualize autonomy alliances and data care practices. These are collective efforts that attempt to subvert inaccessible and autonomy-undermining public digital infrastructures. Drawing on a relational view of autonomy, we examine how certain design choices can constrain citizens’ personal autonomy and equal access to welfare services. For this reason, we discuss the importance of studying political decisions affecting the design and organization of digital welfare services, as well as the local practices that compensate for discriminatory design choices through social inclusion and a commitment to equity.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nino Carreras, Barbara","Finken, Sisse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382152"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital Inclusion","Digital welfare","Equity","Inaccessibility","Public library","Relational autonomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomy alliances and data care practices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93608805/NinoCarrerasFinken_AutonomyAlliances_PDF_213_KB.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382152","identifier":[{"id":"85138000310","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3c7a1101-1b55-4c43-9c10-882f7aa4af57"],"keyword":["digital inclusion","digital welfare","equity","inaccessibility","public library","relational autonomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-F84B934B688E73F4BB8E003353F7173F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/93608805/NinoCarrerasFinken_AutonomyAlliances_PDF_213_KB.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"ninocarreraspau","last":"Nino Carreras","name":"Nino Carreras, Barbara","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sisse","key":"finkenpau","last":"Finken","locid":"70f3c85a-9cd2-40b4-bed9-5e2a75609421","name":"Finken, Sisse","orcid":"0000-0001-7792-7216","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-15688-5_5","eisbn":["https://doi.org/10.1007/9783031156885_5"],"pages":"47-57","status":"p","subtitle":"HCC 2022: Human Choice and Digital by Default: Autonomy vs Digital Determination","title":"IFIP International Conference on Human Choice and Computers"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138000310"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3c7a1101-1b55-4c43-9c10-882f7aa4af57"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Autonomy Alliances and Data Care Practices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382152","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Reporting from an ethnographic study on municipal welfare provision, we focus on care workers’ “data discipline” when engaging in result-documentation within rehabilitation work. We show how the care workers’ own approach to result- documentation is a different kind of “data discipline” than the one called for by municipal management and supplemented by the digital care record. To unfold the analysis we draw on insights from Science and Technology Studies and Computer Supported Cooperative Work. We conclude the paper arguing that “data discipline” is practiced by care workers, they, however, engage in a different kind of data discipline.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Enslev, Lea","Finken, Sisse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382974"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data discipline","Ethnographic study","Municipal welfare provision","Rehabilitation work","Science and Technology Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on data discipline citizen care records and rehabilitation work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18420/ihc2021_011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382974","ids":["itu-7364ee8f-ca97-4f9d-936b-d3767c57943d"],"keyword":["Data discipline","Ethnographic study","Municipal welfare provision","Rehabilitation work","Science and Technology Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6985C195F43CF4E44E219257475A456D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18420/ihc2021_011","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86228674/infraHEALTH_2021_paper_11.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.eusset.eu/handle/20.500.12015/4180","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lea","key":"enslevpau","last":"Enslev","name":"Enslev, Lea","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sisse","key":"finkenpau","last":"Finken","locid":"70f3c85a-9cd2-40b4-bed9-5e2a75609421","name":"Finken, Sisse","orcid":"0000-0001-7792-7216","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18420/ihc2021_011","edition":"4","place":"Kristiansand","publisher":"European Society for Socially Embedded Technologies (EUSSET)","status":"p","subtitle":"Digitalization and Personal Health Data","title":"infraHealth 2021: Proceedings of the 8th International Conference on Infrastructures in Healthcare","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7364ee8f-ca97-4f9d-936b-d3767c57943d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On data discipline, citizen care records, and rehabilitation work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382974","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"With the wake of digital welfare, governments advocate that patients play an active role in managing their own illnesses. This active role is sustained by access to and use of health data provided by health care authorities through new digital technologies. Stepping into an empirical site where patients log in to their own site, ‘MyChart’, we inquire their practices reading health care data and their imaginaries about active involvement in their own health care. With this, our analysis focuses on the active patient and aims to bring forth local imaginaries in an effort to nuance data imaginaries located in political strategies, which relate data access with active partnerships. Within this, we illustrate how patients are active, while data is silent and in need of work before it vocals meaningful for the patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","Finken, Sisse"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381322"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active patients","Data work","Digital health care","Sociotechnical imaginaries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"silent data active patients","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85520716/LaursenFinken_SilentDataActivePatients_HCC14_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381322","identifier":[{"id":"85097410250","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-043935e3-e491-4058-93a5-3ba41e7cef8f"],"keyword":["Active patients","Data work","Digital health care","Sociotechnical imaginaries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5072B7C5011F28EE580ECCF19DA6E1A0"],"oa_link":[{"